# Project Architecture

`docs/project-specification.md` is the single source of truth. If any document,
comment, or rule conflicts with it, the specification wins.

## Structure

- `src` layout; the only importable package is `sales_call_agent`.
- Subpackages mirror the specification's pipeline: `ingestion` ->
  `transcription` -> `diarization` -> `speaker_identity` -> `evaluation` ->
  `aggregation` (planned), with `rubric` and `knowledge_base` supporting
  evaluation.
- `audio` is a technical subpackage supporting ingestion and transcription, not
  an additional business pipeline stage.
- `aggregation` will own seller/team rollups, trends, averages, and leaderboard
  calculations; `api` will expose results to the future dashboard.

## Layering rules

- `domain` contains core models and business rules only. It must not import
  I/O, database, or framework code (no SQLAlchemy, FastAPI, psycopg).
- Pipeline packages may depend on `domain`, never on `api`.
- `api` (FastAPI) serves uploads, results, review access, and dashboard data.
  It does not orchestrate the pipeline and must not contain business logic.
- Pipeline execution will be handled by queue-triggered workers. Do not add
  queue dependencies or worker code until the phase that needs them.
- Planned infrastructure (documentation only for now): object storage adapter
  for audio assets, queue abstraction and worker entry points, PostgreSQL for
  structured records, pgvector for knowledge-base embeddings.
- All database access goes through `persistence`; other packages must not open
  connections or embed SQL.
- New cross-cutting decisions get an entry in `docs/decisions.md`.
